Error [E0118]: `Val(wanted)` would make a new `wanted`, but `wanted` already holds a value
  --> pattern_hole_reuse_val_binding.jet:5:25
    |
  5 |     same :: code == Val(wanted)
    |                         ^^^^^^
 Why: A payload name after `==` introduces a new name; it does not compare with an existing value
 Fix: Write `Val((wanted))` to compare with the existing value, or pick a new name to bind
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0118
